.TH DOME-XR 1 "2026-10-20" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dome\-xr \- present the DomeD desktop in OpenXR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
dome\-xr [\-\-server URL] [\-\-frames N] [\-\-capture DIR]
        [\-\-report FILE] [\-\-standalone] [\-\-placement N]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connect to the local DomeD bridge and submit live Wayland client textures and shell surfaces to OpenXR. The default mode requests an overlay or transparent blend mode when supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-\-server URL"
DomeD bridge URL, normally http://127.0.0.1:49640.
.TP
.B "\-\-standalone"
Request a primary XR session rather than the default overlay.
.TP
.B "\-\-placement N"
Select the runtime overlay placement.
.TP
.B "\-\-frames N"
Exit after N frames for a bounded diagnostic run.
.TP
.B "\-\-capture DIR"
Save diagnostic client texture captures to DIR; these are not headset eye captures.
.TP
.B "\-\-report FILE"
Write a diagnostic report.
.TP
.B "\-\-help"
Show usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
XR_RUNTIME_JSON selects the OpenXR runtime manifest. Use a runtime that supports the required composition layers.
.SH INTERACTION FEEDBACK
Double-clicking the physical mouse's middle button shows three short
accent-coloured rings contracting onto the current view cursor. The animation
lasts 660 milliseconds and preserves ordinary middle-button events.
The focused window receives a subtle inner accent border, including a separate
edge in each eye for side-by-side stereo windows. Neither effect changes hit
regions or window placement.
.PP
The universal menu always includes File, Edit and Window, including for applications
without native menu exports. Window offers Send Window to Desktop, Send Window
to XR and Show Window on Both, with the current presentation marked.
The universal menu accepts keyboard navigation in XR. Super+F10 opens it;
Up/Down select enabled rows, Left/Right switch headers or navigate submenus,
Enter or Space activates, and Escape closes. A stationary mouse ray does not
replace the keyboard selection.
.SH LAYERED DESKTOPS
Inactive desktops with XR windows appear on deeper, faded dome layers behind
the active desktop. More distant layers are fainter. Only the active desktop
accepts input. Switching desktops brings the selected desktop to the front.
Minimized windows and windows assigned only to the physical desktop are omitted.

.SH PERFORMANCE DIAGNOSTICS
The source distribution includes scripts/smoke-xr-performance.py. During an
existing DomeD/WiVRn Pro session, run it with --seconds 60 to collect a read-only
performance sample. --output selects the JSON report and --feed selects a custom
runtime performance feed. No headset restart or scene modification is performed.
.PP
CPU percentages use one core as 100 percent. Latency percentiles summarize sampled
gauges rather than every frame. Application GPU timings do not measure the
runtime's layer-squashing GPU work. Concurrent applications affect results.
.PP
WiVRn Pro builds containing the desktop-layer minification patch provide
WIVRN_LAYER_FILTER=balanced or quality on the runtime server. Filtering is off
by default and does not change gaze-driven encoding. It improves minification
quality at additional GPU cost; it is not a performance optimization. Leave it
off when current readability is acceptable. Synthetic shader timings do not
establish full-headset performance. See wivrn-layer-filter(7).
.SH SEE ALSO
dome\-compositor(1), dome\-preview(1)
